 "about": "Historical sites and cultures of undivided India that lie outside India today, by which a live-research write-back naming one of them with its present country (Chanhu-daro, Pakistan) is read as the subcontinent's history, not as practice abroad (decision 0159). Sites are the Wikidata items that are part of, or of the culture of, the Indus Valley Civilization (Q42534) or Gandhara (Q213651) in Pakistan, Afghanistan or Bangladesh, and the archaeological sites (Q839954) and ancient cities (Q15661340) of Pakistan and Bangladesh, with their English labels and aliases, read by the query below on 2026-11-23. A name shorter than four letters, made only of ordinary English words (english_words.scowl.txt), already listed, or only the item's id (no English label) is left out. Cultures are the two with their Wikidata labels and aliases (IVC, under four letters, left out); Gandhara's countries are its Wikidata description's (north-west Pakistan and north-east Afghanistan). Wikidata is CC0. Re-vendored by running the query again, never edited by hand.",
